  "deviations": [
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Storage\\Device\\Local::getFileMimeType",
      "php": "mime_content_type(): libmagic and its compiled database of several thousand rules.",
      "reason": "There is no pure-Rust libmagic, and linking the system libmagic would not give PHP's bundled database either. utopia_storage::mime detects the formats storage buckets hold (images, audio, video, archives, documents, fonts) by signature and tells text, JSON, XML, SVG, HTML, PHP and scripts apart as libmagic does; the cases pin every fixture and common format. Content outside that table can get another type than libmagic gives (truncated archives are application/octet-stream in PHP, by signature in Rust), so mime detection is not fuzzed."
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Storage\\Device\\S3::listFiles",
      "php": "A listing entry with a negative numeric <Size> (`-3`) gives a FileInfo with that negative size.",
      "reason": "FileInfo::size is a u64 in Rust; a negative object size is malformed service output, reported as 0."
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Storage\\Device\\Local::deletePath",
      "php": "Subdirectories are recursed into by stripping strlen($root . \"/\") bytes from realpath()'d paths, which only works when the root is already canonical: under a symlinked root (macOS /tmp) PHP recurses into wrong paths, leaves the subdirectories and returns false.",
      "reason": "Rust strips the canonical root instead, so it also works under a symlinked root; with a canonical root (every case, and every Linux deployment) both behave the same."
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Storage\\Validator\\Upload::isValid",
      "php": "is_uploaded_file(): whether the SAPI received the path as an upload of the current request (always false in the CLI, as in the cases).",
      "reason": "Rust has no SAPI upload registry: the HTTP layer gives Upload::new() the paths it stored the request's uploads at, and the default validator accepts none, as PHP's CLI."
    },
    {
      "symbol": "Utopia\\Storage\\Device\\S3::__construct",
      "php": "Without a client, utopia-php/client's cURL adapter with no overall deadline, a 60 s low-speed abort and TCP keepalive, wrapped in Retry with RetryStrategy.",
      "reason": "The default Rust client (s3::HttpClient over hyper, wrapped in s3::Retry with RetryStrategy) has no low-speed watchdog; callers that need one pass their own s3::Client. Requests, signing, retries and responses are the same."
    }
  ],
